UNIT isFinite
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pure predicate. No seam (no clock/RNG/env/io/net). Deterministic on its
# single argument. No mutation, no side effects, no carried data, zero deps.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SIG isFinite(value: any) -> boolean

DEPENDS-ON none

EMISSION-INTERFACE
  # The original unit is the DEFAULT export (module.exports = isFinite).
  # The blind re-emitter MUST `export default <fn>` from the .mjs:
  #     export default function isFinite(value) { ... }
  #   -- or --
  #     function isFinite(value) { ... }
  #     export default isFinite;
  # The harness loads the module via dynamic import() and calls the default
  # export as a unary function. Return value is a strict JS boolean (true/false).

BEHAVIOR
  # The EXACT 3.3.2 implementation (verified by reading index.js AND by running
  # the installed package on every edge below):
  #
  #     var nativeIsFinite = root.isFinite;          # the GLOBAL isFinite, NOT Number.isFinite
  #     function isFinite(value) {
  #       return typeof value == 'number' && nativeIsFinite(value);
  #     }
  #
  # Behavioral contract (this is what the blind re-emitter must satisfy):
  #
  # NODE 1 (type gate, short-circuit AND):
  #   If `typeof value !== 'number'`  -> return false IMMEDIATELY.
  #   Because of the short-circuit, the value is NEVER coerced and the inner
  #   finite-check is never reached for non-number inputs. This is THE
  #   discriminator vs the global `isFinite`: lodash isFinite does NOT coerce.
  #   In particular:
  #     - numeric STRINGS ('3', '0', '1e3', '') -> false   # NOT coerced to a number
  #     - bigint (3n, 0n)                        -> false   # typeof is 'bigint'
  #     - boolean (true, false)                  -> false
  #     - null, undefined (incl. NO ARGUMENT)    -> false
  #     - objects/arrays/RegExp/Set/Map/         -> false
  #       Uint8Array/Buffer/Date/boxed
  #       (new Number/new String/new Boolean)            # typeof is 'object'
  #     - Symbol                                 -> false   # typeof is 'symbol'
  #     - function                               -> false   # typeof is 'function'
  #
  # NODE 2 (finite-number check), reached ONLY when typeof value === 'number':
  #   Return the result of the GLOBAL isFinite applied to the number.
  #   For a value that is already a NUMBER primitive, global isFinite(x) and
  #   Number.isFinite(x) agree exactly (no coercion happens on a number), so:
  #     true  iff x is a finite number primitive
  #     false iff x is NaN, +Infinity, or -Infinity
  #   Concretely:
  #     - any finite number incl. 0, -0, negatives, fractions,
  #       Number.MAX_VALUE, Number.MIN_VALUE, Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER,
  #       1e3, 1e308                              -> true
  #     - NaN                                     -> false
  #     - Infinity / +Infinity / Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY -> false
  #     - -Infinity / Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY    -> false
  #     - a numeric LITERAL that overflows to Infinity at parse time
  #       (e.g. 1e309 === Infinity) is already the number Infinity -> false
  #
  # RESULT TYPE: a primitive boolean. (true && finite-check yields the boolean
  # returned by global isFinite, which is always a primitive boolean; the
  # false branch yields the primitive false from the typeof comparison.)
  # -0 is a finite number -> true (Object.is(-0,-0) irrelevant; value-equal to a
  # finite number, global isFinite(-0) === true).

ORACLE value -> oracle.json
  # Single boolean output graded by strict equality. No seam, no trace.

SCOPE
  IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly):
    - the typeof === 'number' gate (short-circuit, no coercion)
    - the finite check (false for NaN / +-Infinity, true otherwise) on number primitives
  CARRIED DATA: none.
  OUT-OF-CONTRACT: none (no stateful mutators, no side APIs).
  OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (documented, NOT emitted by genInputs because they do not
  survive the input codec's JSON.stringify(encode(args)) round-trip):
    - Symbol  -> behavior is false (typeof 'symbol'); documented here so a blind
      re-emitter reconstructs it, but Symbols are not codec-faithful so the
      generator does not emit them.
    - function values -> behavior is false (typeof 'function'); not codec-faithful,
      not emitted.
    All other JS edge values used by genInputs (RegExp, Set, Map, Uint8Array,
    Buffer, bigint, -0, NaN, +/-Infinity, boxed Number/String/Boolean) ARE
    round-trippable by the factory codec and are exercised explicitly.

